ility). So strong reliability and decision, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect cooperation. So good technical, responsibility, but crew issues.\n\nWe need to compare. Which candidate best overall? Candidate C has reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but unorganized and poor criticism. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric and difficulty communicating could be safety risk. Candidate B's uncooperative also risk. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance also risk.\n\nWe might need more info about communication for Candidate B or D. Could ask other panel members. But we need to make an initial contribution. Perhaps we can start by highlighting Candidate C's strengths and concerns, and propose provisional vote for C, but note need to discuss communication.\n\nThus: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I propose Candidate C as current recommendation, because reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, but note concerns about communication and egocentric attitude that need to be weighed. I ask others for any additional observations on C's communication and teamwork.\n\nWe also need METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
